# Local tool index (Template)

> ⚠️ **This file is a template. Real `tool-index.md` is auto-generated by scripts and gitignored (machine-specific).**

---

## First Run

Generate your local tool index:

```powershell
# Windows (PowerShell)
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.ps1"
```

```bash
# Linux / macOS / Kali
bash skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.sh
```

---

## Generated Format

Windows (PowerShell) emits an 8-column table:
| Tool | Skill | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Source | Script ref |

Linux/macOS (Bash) emits a 7-column table:
| Tool | Skill | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Install hint |

Both include a Capability Status subtable with MCP registration and service-online checks.

